  <SafetyDisclaimerBlock />

  <h2>Why Nutrition Values Are Estimates</h2>
  <p>Every number you see generated by our calculators is an estimation. It is practically impossible to calculate the exact molecular composition of the food on your plate. Values vary significantly due to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Brand formulations:</strong> Different brands use different amounts of oils, sugars, and preservatives.</li>
    <li><strong>Crop and livestock variation:</strong> An apple grown in one region may have slightly different sugar content than an apple grown elsewhere.</li>
    <li><strong>Preparation methods:</strong> Frying, boiling, baking, and trimming fat all alter the final caloric weight and density of food.</li>
    <li><strong>Measurement inaccuracies:</strong> Measuring by volume (like cups or tablespoons) is highly inaccurate compared to weighing in grams.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Source Hierarchy and AI Boundaries</h2>
  <p>We prioritize transparency in where our data originates. We attempt to use the <strong>USDA FoodData Central</strong> as our primary source of truth. When that is unavailable, we fall back to a local dataset of estimates.</p>
  <p><strong>AI Parsing Disclaimer:</strong> We may use Artificial Intelligence to help read messy text (like a block of recipe ingredients). AI can make mistakes. It may misunderstand quantities, units, or brand names. Users must review the items that the AI selects to ensure they match the intended ingredients. The AI does <em>not</em> invent the final math; it only suggests which foods to pull from the database.</p>

  <h2>Allergy and Safety Disclaimer</h2>
  <p><strong>This site does not guarantee allergen safety.</strong> We cannot know if a manufacturer has changed their recipe, or if cross-contamination occurred. If you have severe food allergies or medical dietary restrictions, you must read the physical labels on the products you consume and contact the manufacturers directly.</p>

  <h2>Nutrition Facts-Style Label Preview</h2>
  <p>The visual Nutrition Facts-style labels generated by our Recipe Calculator are for <strong>personal estimation only</strong>. They are not commercial packaging labels. They are not reviewed, certified, or approved by the FDA or any other regulatory body. Do not use these labels for commercial food packaging or sales.</p>

  <h2>No Guarantees</h2>
  <p>We make no guarantees regarding the completeness, accuracy, or continuous availability of the data provided by our tools. Please use the site responsibly and in conjunction with professional guidance.</p>

</TrustPageShell>
